# Optional: `k dev` needs no .env. Two tabs or two browsers on this machine,
# or on one network, reach each other directly, with no STUN or TURN server.
# Copy this to .env (git-ignored) only to try your own TURN server in
# development. `.env` is read only in development; production reads the
# real process environment, and `k test` reads neither. Format:
# docs/design/25-config-and-secrets.md.

# Your coturn, with `--use-auth-secret --static-auth-secret=<the secret>`:
# K_TURN_URLS=turn:localhost:3478?transport=udp,turn:localhost:3478?transport=tcp
# K_TURN_SECRET=change-me
